# Deployment smoke suite — transient run artifacts (not tracked).
# Generated per-run report directories; keep the folder via reports/.gitkeep.
reports/*
!reports/.gitkeep

# Portable diagnostic packages (smoke_package.py): one scrubbed .zip per run,
# built in packages/ (its .staging_* folder is removed after zipping), and the
# main-container inbox/ where --import extracts packages and writes MATRIX.md.
# Both carry run data from other installs, so neither is tracked; keep the
# folders via their .gitkeep (docker cp into inbox/ needs it to exist).
packages/*
!packages/.gitkeep
inbox/*
!inbox/.gitkeep

# Probe sandboxes: each run_tier2() mints a UUID-owned run_<uuid>/ directory
# under _sandbox/, writes only its own T2.1/T2.2 fixtures there, and removes
# exactly that directory in a guaranteed cleanup path (never a recursive wipe of
# _sandbox/ itself). A run_<uuid>/ left behind by a hard process kill is inert
# crash residue — its UUID is never re-minted, so it can never satisfy a future
# run. Two historical 2026-07-15 root fixtures (t21_marker.txt, t22_probe.py)
# predate this per-run design and are non-authoritative. All of _sandbox/ stays
# ignored.
_sandbox/
